;;; Settings-local.scm -- LOCAL, UNTRACKED settings overlay.  COPY THIS FILE to
;;; scm/runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm and edit; the copy is .gitignore'd.
;;; Copyright 2026 by Frobenius Norm LLC
;;;
;;; WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  Settings.scm is tracked, and it rides data/ into the per-target
;;; customer packages that `w3 make publish_one` FORCE-PUSHES to public GitHub repos
;;; (github.com/<user>/LambLispRT-v01-<env>).  So a bench SSID and password typed into
;;; Settings.scm is published to the world on the next release.  Put them here instead:
;;;
;;;   - this name is in .gitignore, so it cannot be committed by accident;
;;;   - manifests pull it with `optional:`, so its absence is silent, not a warning;
;;;   - w3_make_release_one DELETES it from the package, so it cannot ship even if
;;;     it is sitting in data_staged/ when a release is cut.
;;;
;;; Keys here OVERRIDE the same keys in Settings.scm; anything not named here is unchanged.
;;; Read by setup.scm immediately after Settings.scm.

;;; THE VALUES BELOW ARE REAL AND DELIBERATELY PUBLIC (owner, 2026-10-03).  `JetsonWiFi` is the
;;; access point the Jetson appliance runs for the boards on its own wire, and its passphrase is
;;; `Example!` -- chosen to be publishable, so this file can show a WORKING overlay instead of a
;;; placeholder nobody can test against.  Every other bench network we use is private and must
;;; never appear in a published file; see the release scrub in w3_make.sh, which allowlists the
;;; three names a customer has ever received and drops the rest.
((wifi      . 1)                  ;; 1 = auto-connect at boot (needed by the `network` test_id)
 (wifi_ssid . "JetsonWiFi")
 (wifi_pass . "Example!"))
